  "observations": [
    "Keyboard settings/reset retain text, column spacing, action framing and modal hierarchy relative to Stage9.",
    "Gamepad settings retain four columns, values, clear controls and lower actions; existing dense 4:3 spacing shows no new clipping in supplied views.",
    "Pad reset dialog retains readable two-line message and separated reset/cancel actions in all three ratios.",
    "Audio settings retain four label/slider/value rows, explanatory text and save/discard actions. Background world remains faintly visible as in the comparison.",
    "Legacy standalone fixtures show an upper card-collection auxiliary button that actual managed after views hide. This is a fixture/host-context boundary, not evidence that the complete legacy host had this behavior."
  ],
